            9. DJI vs Jackery, EcoFlow, Anker and Bluetti
          </h2>

          <p>
            This guide compares DJI models with each other. The other big brands have their own guides, and the short version is that DJI's strengths are specific.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Where DJI Stands Out</h3>

          <p>
            DJI's listings emphasise fast wall charging, high output for the capacity, quiet operation and drone battery charging. The Power 1000 V2's 2,600W from 1kWh is more output than many rivals of similar size list.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Where Others May Suit You Better</h3>

          <p>
            If you want a built-in solar controller, look at rivals whose specs include one. For larger whole-home systems and 240V output, look at the bigger home units from other brands. See our guides to the <a href="/best-jackery-power-station/">best Jackery power stations</a>, <a href="/best-ecoflow-power-station/">best EcoFlow power stations</a>, <a href="/best-anker-power-station/">best Anker power stations</a> and <a href="/best-bluetti-power-station/">best Bluetti power stations</a>, and our overall <a href="/best-portable-power-station/">best portable power stations</a> roundup.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="warranty" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            10. Warranty, App and Long-Term Care
          </h2>

          <p>
            A power station should last a decade, so the support around it matters.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Warranty Terms</h3>

          <p>
            Most DJI listings here state a 5-year warranty. One Power 1000 V2 bundle listing describes it as 3 years, extendable to 5 with registration. Register the unit with DJI when you buy it, and keep proof of purchase.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">The App</h3>

          <p>
            The Power 2000 listing says it connects wirelessly to the DJI Home app without the separate DJI Power Dongle. Check your model's listing for app support before relying on remote monitoring.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Storage Between Outages</h3>

          <p>
            LFP batteries tolerate storage well. Keep the station somewhere cool and dry, store it partly charged if it will sit for months, and top it up every few months so it is ready when the power goes out.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="generator" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            11. Is a DJI Power Station a Generator?
          </h2>

          <p>
            People search for a DJI generator, and DJI's own listings call these units electric or solar generators. They are battery power stations: they store energy rather than burning fuel to make it.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">What That Means Indoors</h3>

          <p>
            A power station produces no exhaust, so you can use it inside the home, unlike a gas generator, which must stay outdoors and away from windows. Give it ventilation, keep it dry and away from heat, and follow DJI's safety instructions. Our guide to <a href="/are-portable-power-stations-safe-indoors/">whether power stations are safe indoors</a> covers the details.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">The Trade-Off</h3>

          <p>
            A gas generator runs as long as you have fuel; a power station runs until the battery is empty, then needs the grid, solar or a car to recharge. For long outages, many households pair a power station with panels or keep a fuel generator as a second line. See <a href="/portable-power-station-vs-generator/">portable power station vs generator</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

